## 0 · Findings that come before any design (measured today)

| # | Finding | Evidence | Consequence |
|---|---|---|---|
| F-A | **The door does not know v4.** `jev-boundary markers` lists 52 markers and 0 contain `hee4` or `v4`. Its roots are all v3 or planning paths. The synthetic line `please plan the hee4 roadmap in ~/hee4-evidence/design` piped to `jev-boundary text` returned **rc=0**, which means "send". | `jev-boundary markers`, `jev-boundary text` run 2026-10-01 | Every decision below that puts prompt text in its state is **unsafe in a v4 session** until the door learns the v4 roots and markers (`~/hee4-evidence`, the v4 codebase root `~/herdr-engineering-engine-v4`, and the `hee4` runtime namespace: `~/.local/state/hee4/`, `~/.config/hee4/`, `~/.local/lib/hee4/`, `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hee4/` *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-11)*). This is prerequisite P0. |
| F-B | **Suspected leak through the Stop verifier.** 5 of the 5 `block_fail` rows for this session were sent from cwd `~` with claim heads about HEE work, for example "Main is pushed. GitHub `main` is now `b5367bc`…". The verifier's engine check keys on paths and cwd, so a *report about* engine work written from `$HOME` passes. | `~/.local/state/jev-verifier/verdicts.jsonl`: this session had `not_sent=29 no_claim=15 block_fail=5` | The scope box forbids reports and task context (FINAL.md:87). This is **suspected, not adjudicated**: whether a commit sha plus "pushed" counts as a report is Luke's call. The design must not copy the pattern. *(rev 2026-10-01, V2: verification re-read the 5 rows; engine report text did reach the verifier's Jev call, so the send is a fact. Whether it breaches the scope box is still Luke's ruling, prerequisite P2 in §5.)* |
| F-C | **The read gate's question is built from the task.** Its instruction interpolates `"$task"` into the question string (`Assimilating…:59`), and the task comes from the charter (`:135`). That breaks "question text fixed, never derived from a task". The fix is to keep the question fixed and move the charter into `state.task_charter`. *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V10 row 19)* **Restated against the installed hook:** this finding describes the bash quoted in the jev.vault note, not the gate that runs. The installed `~/.claude/hooks/jev-read-gate-guard.sh` (mtime 2026-09-30 15:19) defines a constant `QUESTION` at `:70` and puts the charter into **state** at `:166` (`{"task": task, "content": c}`); `grep -c '$task'` over the hook → 0 (re-read 2026-10-01). | source quoted in the note | ~~This is a redesign item for the existing gate (P1), not new work.~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V10 row 19)* JP1 is already met in code; ATLAS H-20 is closed by that read-back. No redesign item remains for the installed gate. |
| F-D | **All 5 CONTRADICTED events this session are relay-shaped.** Each had `tests_run_count=0` and `test_exit_code=null`, and each fired on `output_contradicts` (0.63–0.84) with `gaps` mostly `undisclosed`. They are claims relayed from a push or a subagent with no check the verifier could see in the transcript. Across the whole log there were 165 rows: `not_sent 80 · no_claim 51 · rerun 20 · block_fail 10 · report_pass 4`. | verdicts.jsonl | The relay decision (Q5) targets a real, recurring shape. The rows are **unlabelled**, so the true rate of unchecked relays is UNMEASURED: some of these may be verifier false positives. |
| F-E | **No labels exist anywhere yet.** Recall `cards` labels = 0. There are 0 falsifier labels. The router has 65 decisions (`set 5 / advise 49 / none 11`) and 0 labels. | `jev-recall/memory.json`; `Round 6…:110` | "Labelled set before unattended" is unmet for every installed Jev hook, so no new decision point can inherit a threshold from them. |
| F-F | **The L3 preview trap.** `jev-axi filter` sends 600 chars per item by default. On one corpus it kept 0/8 true items, while grep found 8/8 in 40 ms. | `Assimilating…:17`, `:146-148` | Every state below states its byte size. No door's default acquisition is used unsized. |

