## 3 · Where Jev must NOT be used

*(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V10 row 15)* **Jaggedness has 9 numbered weaknesses**, settled from the live docs (`docs.typesafe.ai/model-jaggedness/jev-1.13.md`, headings `1. Literal reading` … `9. Generation`, last reviewed 2026-09-17). Item 2, *Math and Numbers*, has three subsections (Counting, Numeric representations, Math using score); the jev.vault note's "11 items" counted two of them as items. The row numbers below are the 9 items.

| Never | Why (source) | Instead |
|---|---|---|
| Arithmetic, counts, line counts, token totals, "is N of M complete" | Jaggedness row 2 (`10 Model/Jaggedness jev-1.13.md:16`; rows 2/3/8/9 were cited one line early, *rev 2026-10-01, V2 fix 10*). p5 `jev-ledger` **BACKED three arithmetically false claims** (Round 4:35) | code |
| Dates, recency, "the latest handover" | Jaggedness row 3 (:17, *rev 2026-10-01*). L4: right answer at 0.32 vs 0.29, unactionable (Assimilating:18). Calibration maps port catastrophically, ECE 0.083 → 0.909 (Schematics:97) | `ls -t`, code |
| Exact lookups: does string X appear, where is symbol Y defined | L3 and E10-7's miss at 0.81 (Level 10:45) | grep |
| Set membership: paths, allow-lists, engine or non-engine | Schematics:98 | code, the door |
| Anything the door marks, and **any HEE task context even when the door passes it** (F-A, F-B): v4 prompts, Claude's drafts and subagent returns in HEE sessions, commit shas, gate output | FINAL.md:87; Engine Data Grant:22 | code-only features; log `not_sent` |
| Writing the answer (generation) | Jaggedness row 9 (:23, *rev 2026-10-01*) | Claude |
| Deciding which command to run, or discovering dependencies over N² pairs | p4 recall 0.25/0.0 (Round 4:37) | code enumerates; Jev checks declared items |
| Carrying one threshold across families, or across a Noul and a Choice | Jaggedness row 8 (:22); Confidence:35 *(rev 2026-10-01, V2 fix 10)* | a threshold per question id |
| Anything that reads an approval field | Router:35 (no approval field wired) | `user_words` only |

