## 5 · Staged rollout (every stage after S0 needs Luke's "start coding")

| Stage | What | Exit line that must print |
|---|---|---|
| S0 (now) | This document; question texts frozen above | — |
| S1 | **P0** v4 markers and roots in `jev-boundary`, with a control: the synthetic v4 line → rc 3. **P1** read-gate question fixed. **P2** Luke's ruling on F-B, and the verifier refusing report-shaped claims about engine work. All three are staged diffs Luke applies, because the classifier refuses edits to steering files (Round 6:93) | `jev-boundary` control `rc=3`; `habitat-reflex verify` `unproven=0` |
| S2 | Offline: Q1/Q2/Q3/Q5 packs through `jev-exemplar-run` on 40 synthetic cases plus 16 held-out from another head, with a paraphrase pass and adversarial cases (a spoofed opt-in, a "note to the router") | held-out ≥ 14/16, adversarial all, code-baseline column printed; else one revision, then stop |
| S3 | Shadow hook, log only, folded into the recall call, for ≥ 50 prompts in non-engine sessions | agreement matrix, `labels=N`, `usd`, `ms p50/p95`; `UNMEASURED` rows counted |
| S4 | Advisory: one line per turn, only for ASK, MEASURE_FIRST and relay-belay, raw p quoted | Wilson lower ≥ 0.85 per id; falsifier dated |
| — | **Enforcement is not planned.** The shape of an answer stays Claude's decision; Jev only advises. Engine sessions stay code-only until a scoped grant | — |

Related: `jev.vault/60 Habitat/HEE Decision Points and Jev Candidates 2026-10-01.md` (A1–A6, the engine-side J1–J14)
· `80 Schematics/Jev in Claude Code - Schematics 2026-09-29.md` §4 matrix. Public pattern pages were read
2026-10-01 through WebFetch summaries (not verbatim):
[intent-routing](https://docs.typesafe.ai/patterns/intent-routing.md) routes to a human below 0.5 intent confidence;
[confidence-routing](https://docs.typesafe.ai/patterns/confidence-routing.md) uses a 0.6 floor, thresholds scaled to
stakes, and > 0.85 for high risk. ~~Those pages support the 0.60 advisory lines above for low-stakes advice.~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V10 row 20)* They do not: the 0.6 and 0.5 lines gate a **Choice `confidence`**, and Q1/Q2 read a **Noul `p`**, which has no confidence. Carrying a threshold across primitives is what §3 forbids (jaggedness item 8). **The Noul cut is derived from labels:** for each question id, the lowest p at which the Wilson lower bound on precision is ≥ 0.85 over ≥ 10 labelled cases (S4's bar). Until those labels exist, the 0.60 lines are provisional and UNMEASURED, and they stay advisory.
